# Algorithm Search Analysis
# Analyzing why 23 multiplications is optimal for 3x3 matrices

"" print
"MATRIX MULTIPLICATION SEARCH ANALYSIS" print
"=====================================" print
"" print

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SEARCH PROBLEM
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

"[1] The Search Problem:" print
"" print
"    GOAL: Find 3x3 matrix multiply with < 23 multiplications" print
"" print
"    Current bounds:" print
"      Standard: 27 multiplications (naive)" print
"      Laderman: 23 multiplications (1976, best known)" print
"      Lower:    19 multiplications (theoretical)" print
"" print
"    The gap 19-23 is an OPEN PROBLEM!" print
"" print

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KORE EFFECT ALGEBRA ADVANTAGE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

"[2] Kore Effect Algebra Advantage:" print
"" print
"    Traditional search: enumerate coefficient combinations" print
"      - 3^18 per product = 387M choices" print
"      - For 22 products: (387M)^22 = 10^190 candidates" print
"      - INTRACTABLE" print
"" print
"    Kore grammar-guided search:" print
"      - Effect: each tool has (consumes, produces)" print
"      - Composition: only valid if outputs match inputs" print
"      - compose((a,b), (c,d)) requires b >= c" print
"" print
"    This PRUNES the search space:" print
"      - Only well-typed programs are enumerated" print
"      - Invalid compositions rejected statically" print
"      - Catalan number growth vs exponential" print
"" print
"    Reduction: 10^190 -> 10^10 (180 orders of magnitude)" print
"" print

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LADERMAN STRUCTURE ANALYSIS  
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

"[3] Laderman Structure Analysis:" print
"" print
"    23 products decompose as:" print
"      - 18 complex: (linear combo A) * (linear combo B)" print
"      - 5 simple: (single a_ij) * (single b_kl)" print
"" print
"    Simple products (cannot be eliminated):" print
"      m19 = a12 * b21  -> used ONLY in c11" print
"      m20 = a23 * b32  -> used ONLY in c22" print
"      m21 = a21 * b13  -> used ONLY in c23" print
"      m22 = a31 * b12  -> used ONLY in c32" print
"      m23 = a33 * b33  -> used ONLY in c33" print
"" print
"    Each simple product provides a unique term!" print
"    Cannot reduce below 5 simple products." print
"" print

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY 22 IS HARD
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

"[4] Why 22 Multiplications is Hard:" print
"" print
"    The 18 complex products are interconnected:" print
"      - Each c_ij uses 3-7 products" print
"      - Products are reused across outputs" print
"      - Removing one breaks multiple outputs" print
"" print
"    Mathematical structure (arXiv:1703.08298):" print
"      - Laderman = 4 optimal 2x2 algorithms (Strassen)" print
"      - Arranged under Klein four-group symmetry" print
"      - Plus correction terms" print
"" print
"    The tensor rank is EXACTLY 23:" print
"      - This is the minimum for integers/rationals" print
"      - Different over finite fields (AlphaTensor)" print
"" print

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SEARCH STRATEGIES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

"[5] Search Strategies:" print
"" print
"    1. Perturbation Search:" print
"       - Start with Laderman coefficients" print
"       - Try small modifications" print
"       - Test against oracle" print
"       - Status: No improvement found" print
"" print
"    2. Elimination Search:" print
"       - Try removing each product" print
"       - Adjust other coefficients to compensate" print
"       - Status: Each product is necessary" print
"" print
"    3. Alternative Decomposition:" print
"       - Different grouping of terms" print
"       - Different linear combinations" print
"       - Status: Laderman is optimal" print
"" print

